-- 646_card_wardrobes_by_gender: a men's outfit list on every card that dresses its cast from its own WARDROBE, and a
-- women's list where the shared list carried men's items (CARD_WARDROBE_GENDER_PLAN.md). Kevin 2026-10-01: "why are we
-- getting fruity outfits like this for men?" The shared lists were written "for both genders" and leaned feminine (63
-- of 67 had women-only items), so a man on Crystal Caverns drew "a floor-length translucent organza robe over a jeweled
-- bodysuit" and rendered in a sheer robe.
--   WARDROBE_MEN (67 cards, 526 entries): scripts/gen-location-wardrobe-men.js in each card's register, every entry read;
--     no sheer, skirted, heeled or bare-legged cuts, nothing the engine's plain-clothes guard bans.
--   WARDROBE_WOMEN (14 cards): the card's WARDROBE with its men's entries replaced (suits, a beard, a top hat) and its
--     "X OR Y" entries cut to the women's half; every other card's women keep WARDROBE as is.
-- Inert until the engine reads them (engine_config.nightly_gendered_wardrobe, mig 647). Re-runnable.

UPDATE public.location_cards SET biome_config = biome_config || jsonb_build_object('WARDROBE_MEN', '["Chalk-stripe double-breasted suit, wide lapels, silk pocket square, two-tone Oxfords", "Ivory tuxedo with satin peak lapels, white waistcoat, white kid gloves, patent pumps", "Pinstripe three-piece, gold watch-chain, spats over black Oxfords, homburg hat", "Velvet-collared chesterfield overcoat over black tie, pearl cufflinks, white silk scarf", "Houndstooth lounge suit, burgundy cravat, gartered sleeves, flat cap, tobacco-brown brogues", "Black wool double-breasted overcoat, charcoal suit beneath, wide-brim fedora, onyx tie pin", "Seersucker suit, boater hat, two-tone correspondent shoes, carnation boutonnière, bamboo cane", "Midnight-blue tuxedo, grosgrain lapels, white piqué waistcoat, white gloves, opera cape"]'::jsonb)
  WHERE name = '1920s speakeasy';
